{% comment %}
  Ingredient button artwork, lifted straight from Santosh's "KCC Ingredient
  Buttons.svg" (the 9-circle layout in KCC Website/). Every symbol below is that
  file's own named layer, extracted programmatically from the file rather than
  transcribed, so the icon in each slot is the one the artwork is actually
  labelled as.

  Source layer -> symbol handle:
    Cardamom             -> cardamom
    Star-Anise           -> star-anise
    Black-Pepper         -> pepper
    Cloves               -> cloves
    Cinnamon             -> cinnamon
    Carom-Seeds--Ajwain- -> carom
    Ginger               -> ginger
    Coffee-Beans         -> coffee
    Black-Tea            -> tea

  One thing worth knowing about the source art: there is no fennel in it. The
  ninth drawing is labelled
     "Carom Seeds (Ajwain)". It's mapped to the Fennel block because the two
     look near-identical (small ridged seeds) and nothing else fits; rename the
     block to "Carom seeds" if you'd rather the copy match the drawing.

  Ginger and Cinnamon were redrawn as vectors by Santosh and re-extracted on
  2026-10-21; they used to be embedded raster PNGs in the artwork and went soft
  the moment they were scaled past the button. Every symbol here is line art
  now. Regenerate any of them with:

      python3 scripts/build-ingredient-icons.py <Layer-Id> <handle>

  Framing: each symbol's viewBox is its button's ring (a 50x50 circle, identical
  for all nine), NOT a tight box around its own artwork. That preserves how full
  each circle is in the original (~90-100%) and the relative sizes between icons.
  Tea and star anise overflow the ring slightly by design, so the <svg> that
  references these is overflow:visible.

  Rendered once per section as a hidden sprite; ingredient-icon.liquid then
  references a symbol with <use>. That keeps the artwork out of the markup 18
  times over (9 buttons + 9 illustration panels). Symbol ids are namespaced with
  the section id so two of these sections on one page can't collide.

  Colour: the per-path fills (all rgb(205,100,62) in the source) were stripped and
  replaced with a single fill="currentColor" on each symbol, so these inherit
  colour the same way the theme's other icons do.

  Accepts: uid (required) - unique per section, use section.id
{% endcomment %}

<svg
  class="ingredient-icon-sprite"
  aria-hidden="true"
  focusable="false"
  xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"
  xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink"
  style="position:absolute;width:0;height:0;overflow:hidden"
>
  <defs>
